{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git diff --stat; git status --short; cat ANSWERS.md'","aggregated_output":"?? ANSWERS.md\n## Q1\n\nShipping is free for orders worth **€60.00 or more after discounts**, to a supported EU destination. The comparison includes exactly €60.00; unsupported destinations are rejected before the free-shipping check. Sources: `parcels/settings.py:14-15`, `parcels/quote.py:25-32`, `parcels/carriers.py:22-24`.\n\nChange the threshold without editing code by setting the environment variable `PARCELS_FREE_FROM`, for example `PARCELS_FREE_FROM=75.00 python -m parcels 75.00 3.2 DE`. Settings are read once when the module is imported, so set it before starting the process, or restart an existing process with the new value. Source: `parcels/settings.py:1-15`.\n\n## Q2\n\nAn overweight order is split into the fewest possible equal-weight parcels, using `ceil(total weight / 31.5 kg)`. Each parcel's weight is rounded upward to the nearest gram. For example, 70 kg becomes three parcels of 23.334 kg each. Sources: `parcels/settings.py:17`, `parcels/packing.py:11-22`.\n\nWhen shipping is chargeable, the price is calculated for each parcel and summed; each parcel incurs its own base price, charge per started kilogram, and applicable EU surcharge. Orders meeting the free-shipping threshold return zero before packing or pricing is called. Source: `parcels/quote.py:17-33`.\n\n## Q3\n\nThe default carrier is **PostNL** (`postnl`). Select another carrier by setting `PARCELS_CARRIER` before starting the process, for example `PARCELS_CARRIER=dhl python -m parcels 45.00 3.2 DE`. Allowed values are `dhl`, `ups`, and `postnl`; input is lowercased, so selection is case-insensitive. An unrecognized value raises `RuntimeError` during import. Settings are read only once at import. Source: `parcels/settings.py:1-12`.\n\nThe selected carrier chooses the tariff used to price each parcel. Sources: `parcels/quote.py:10-19`, `parcels/carriers.py:16-20`.\n\n## Q4\n\nFor an order placed on **Friday at 17:00**, the 15:00 cutoff has passed, so the starting date advances by one calendar day to Saturday. The function then adds **one handling day plus the destination's transit days**, counting only weekdays after that starting date. Sources: `parcels/delivery.py:9-11`, `parcels/delivery.py:25-30`, `parcels/settings.py:18`.\n\nThe result depends on the destination:\n\n| Destination | Handling + transit | Delivery after that Friday |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Netherlands (`NL`) | 1 + 1 = 2 working days | Tuesday |\n| Belgium, Germany, Luxembourg (`BE`, `DE`, `LU`) | 1 + 2 = 3 working days | Wednesday |\n| Other supported destinations | 1 + 4 = 5 working days | Friday of the following week |\n\nSources: `parcels/delivery.py:9-10`, `parcels/delivery.py:14-22`, `parcels/delivery.py:25-30`, `parcels/settings.py:18`.\n\n**Weekends are skipped; public holidays are not.** The working-day check only tests whether the weekday is Monday through Friday, so a weekday public holiday still counts toward delivery. The calculation uses the supplied datetime's date and hour without timezone conversion. Source: `parcels/delivery.py:14-30`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
